    "evidence_text": "Minnesota State High School Mathematics League\n\nThe Minnesota State High School Mathematics League is the premier high school mathematics league in the state of Minnesota.\n\n It was founded in 1980 by Macalester College professor Wayne Roberts.\n\n In 2001, the College officially became a coeducational institution.\n\nWells College\n\nGustavus Adolphus College ( ) is a private, coeducational liberal arts college.\n\n The college was founded as the Oberlin Collegiate Institute in 1833 by John Jay Shipherd and Philo Stewart.\n\n It is the oldest coeducational liberal arts college in the United States and the second oldest continuously operating coeducational institute of higher learning in the world.\n\nMinnesota State High School League\n\nThe Minnesota State High School League (MSHSL) is a voluntary, non-profit association for the support and governance of interscholastic activities at high schools in Minnesota, United States.\n\nMacalester College ( ) is a private, coeducational liberal arts college located in Saint Paul, Minnesota, US.\n\n It was founded in 1874 as a Presbyterian-affiliated but nonsectarian college.\n\nThe Suburban East Conference is a Minnesota State High School League conference in the Twin Cities, Minnesota.",
